1
00:01:46,727 --> 00:01:47,879
It's time.

2
00:02:13,415 --> 00:02:15,047
Pillow fight!

3
00:02:41,959 --> 00:02:43,735
Into bed.

4
00:02:43,815 --> 00:02:45,607
Lights out.

5
00:02:55,559 --> 00:02:57,511
Come on. Quickly!

6
00:03:28,199 --> 00:03:29,911
It's dark...

7
00:03:29,991 --> 00:03:31,207
but I'm not afraid.

8
00:03:38,631 --> 00:03:40,263
He's escaping.

9
00:03:45,575 --> 00:03:47,383
There's nothing to fear.

10
00:03:47,463 --> 00:03:49,351
I'm almost there.

11
00:04:17,703 --> 00:04:19,511
There he goes again.

12
00:04:19,591 --> 00:04:22,983
Some night, you're gonna get caught, Tim!

13
00:04:24,135 --> 00:04:25,575
Hi, Adhara.

14
00:05:03,207 --> 00:05:06,823
Hey, everybody, Bobby peed in his bed.

15
00:05:07,431 --> 00:05:08,407
Shut up!

16
00:05:08,487 --> 00:05:10,935
I'm missing a sock. Who took it?

17
00:05:11,015 --> 00:05:12,887
Yeah, like somebody would want...

18
00:05:12,967 --> 00:05:14,759
your smelly old sock!

19
00:05:48,391 --> 00:05:50,695
Hey! That's mine!

20
00:06:28,551 --> 00:06:29,847
10 points!

21
00:06:29,927 --> 00:06:32,423
You're gonna get it!

22
00:06:54,375 --> 00:06:55,559
Wow!

23
00:07:06,887 --> 00:07:09,383
1,2,3.

24
00:07:17,383 --> 00:07:19,431
- Hey, pass it! - Yeah!

25
00:07:20,647 --> 00:07:23,335
It's Tim. He'll never make it.

26
00:07:27,591 --> 00:07:30,103
Oh, no! Look what he did.

27
00:07:30,183 --> 00:07:31,927
Tim, you klutz!

28
00:07:32,007 --> 00:07:33,383
Sorry!

29
00:07:36,839 --> 00:07:38,359
Now you really messed up.

30
00:07:38,439 --> 00:07:40,343
Go get the ball, quick!

31
00:07:40,423 --> 00:07:41,559
I'm trying.

32
00:07:41,639 --> 00:07:43,175
Get it! Get it, Tim!

33
00:07:51,847 --> 00:07:53,303
It's in the basement.

34
00:07:53,383 --> 00:07:54,551
I'm not going down there.

35
00:07:54,631 --> 00:07:57,399
He's kicked it into the basement.
Now what?

36
00:07:57,479 --> 00:07:58,935
Who's gonna get it?

37
00:07:59,015 --> 00:08:00,023
He kicked it down there.

38
00:08:00,103 --> 00:08:01,303
He's got to go get it!

39
00:08:01,383 --> 00:08:03,575
Come on, scaredy-cat!

40
00:08:03,655 --> 00:08:06,119
I can't. There's no light.

41
00:08:06,215 --> 00:08:09,095
Come on! I can see the ball from here.

42
00:08:14,727 --> 00:08:17,207
You'd better have that ball
when you come back...

43
00:08:17,287 --> 00:08:18,839
or you'll be in trouble.

44
00:08:18,919 --> 00:08:21,271
Don't you dare come back without it!

45
00:08:21,351 --> 00:08:24,391
Let's see how he gets out of this one.

46
00:09:02,439 --> 00:09:03,847
Where is it?

47
00:09:06,119 --> 00:09:07,463
Who took it?

48
00:09:08,839 --> 00:09:10,855
Give it back to me!

49
00:09:20,967 --> 00:09:23,847
What's the matter? Afraid of the dark?

50
00:09:55,143 --> 00:09:56,871
At last.

51
00:10:07,591 --> 00:10:08,919
Where are you, Adhara?

52
00:10:08,999 --> 00:10:12,295
From here, I don't know where you are.

53
00:10:14,183 --> 00:10:15,767
Let's see...

54
00:10:15,847 --> 00:10:18,535
There's the North Star.

55
00:10:19,655 --> 00:10:23,095
A bit further down is the Little Dipper.

56
00:10:23,175 --> 00:10:26,327
Pegasus galloping beside the unicorn...

57
00:10:26,407 --> 00:10:29,943
Draco running away from Perseus...

58
00:10:30,023 --> 00:10:34,439
And between Orion and the two canis...

59
00:10:34,599 --> 00:10:36,247
Lepus...

60
00:10:36,327 --> 00:10:38,295
it should be right...

61
00:10:38,375 --> 00:10:39,911
there!

62
00:10:41,511 --> 00:10:43,463
Hi, Adhara!

63
00:10:45,191 --> 00:10:47,399
What's happening?

64
00:10:52,071 --> 00:10:53,479
That's impos...

65
00:11:19,815 --> 00:11:22,311
See? It's not a yellow bat.

66
00:11:28,007 --> 00:11:29,335
It's a boy!

67
00:11:29,415 --> 00:11:31,143
Are these real?

68
00:11:35,207 --> 00:11:37,847
A very rude boy.

69
00:11:37,927 --> 00:11:39,927
Sorry. Thank...

70
00:11:40,007 --> 00:11:42,279
Thank you for saving me.

71
00:11:44,487 --> 00:11:45,559
Hey!

72
00:11:45,639 --> 00:11:46,711
Steady on!

73
00:11:46,791 --> 00:11:49,111
Listen. The stars...

74
00:11:49,191 --> 00:11:50,999
Now, let's see.

75
00:11:51,079 --> 00:11:54,855
Which one of you is responsible
for this boy?

76
00:12:01,191 --> 00:12:03,175
There you are.

77
00:12:09,191 --> 00:12:10,231
Tobermory.

78
00:12:10,311 --> 00:12:11,751
I should have guessed.

79
00:12:12,455 --> 00:12:14,359
Why is this kid still awake?

80
00:12:14,439 --> 00:12:15,575
You were napping again.

81
00:12:15,655 --> 00:12:17,591
Can't you do your job right for once?

82
00:12:17,671 --> 00:12:19,607
Why are you talking to the cats?

83
00:12:19,687 --> 00:12:21,271
Why don't you just ask me?

84
00:12:21,351 --> 00:12:23,095
And who are you?

85
00:12:23,175 --> 00:12:25,143
I'm... I'm Tim.

86
00:12:25,223 --> 00:12:26,743
What...

87
00:12:26,823 --> 00:12:28,055
Who are you?

88
00:12:28,135 --> 00:12:30,135
Do these cats belong to you?

89
00:12:30,215 --> 00:12:32,567
Why do you think
I'm called the cat shepherd?

90
00:12:32,647 --> 00:12:34,071
Tobermory, make him go to sleep.

91
00:12:34,151 --> 00:12:36,567
And you be a good boy and get into bed.

92
00:12:36,647 --> 00:12:38,487
But that's what I was trying to tell you!

93
00:12:38,567 --> 00:12:40,471
I can't go to bed because the window...

94
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:42,295
doesn't open, and I came out here...

95
00:12:42,375 --> 00:12:44,183
and now there's a star missing...

96
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:46,167
so I can't go to sleep.

97
00:12:46,247 --> 00:12:47,895
What's that? What's missing?

98
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:49,511
My star!

99
00:12:50,279 --> 00:12:53,175
Look. Come here.

100
00:12:53,255 --> 00:12:55,367
There's my star, Adhara.

101
00:12:56,359 --> 00:12:58,135
And now look up.

102
00:12:58,215 --> 00:13:00,999
You see? It's not there anymore.

103
00:13:04,935 --> 00:13:06,295
I can fix that.

104
00:13:06,375 --> 00:13:07,751
You can?

105
00:13:09,223 --> 00:13:10,711
There. Now, off to bed!

106
00:13:10,791 --> 00:13:14,215
But I can't go to bed
until my star is back.

107
00:13:15,207 --> 00:13:16,695
Another one just went!

108
00:13:16,775 --> 00:13:18,391
Aren't we gonna do anything?

109
00:13:18,471 --> 00:13:20,471
"We"? Sorry. Not in my job description.

110
00:13:20,551 --> 00:13:21,687
That's Moka.

111
00:13:21,767 --> 00:13:22,935
Moka? Who's Moka?

112
00:13:23,015 --> 00:13:24,855
Does he know about the stars?

113
00:13:24,935 --> 00:13:27,383
Of all the stubborn, obstinate,
irritating little...

114
00:13:27,463 --> 00:13:28,983
He's the boss, the big guy...

115
00:13:29,063 --> 00:13:30,967
the head honcho who runs Nocturna.

116
00:13:31,047 --> 00:13:33,383
Nocturna? What's Nocturna?

117
00:13:34,727 --> 00:13:38,103
Don't you realize I'm a very busy man?

118
00:13:38,183 --> 00:13:40,151
It's not easy being a cat shepherd.

119
00:13:40,231 --> 00:13:41,943
I have responsibilities!

120
00:13:42,023 --> 00:13:44,760
I have to tell this Moka
about the missing star!

121
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,615
Impossible. Moka never sees visitors.

122
00:13:46,695 --> 00:13:48,215
He will see me!

123
00:13:48,295 --> 00:13:49,703
He's far too important!

124
00:13:54,823 --> 00:13:55,735
That cat!

125
00:13:55,815 --> 00:13:58,967
I'm giving you one more chance, Tobermory.

126
00:13:59,047 --> 00:14:00,439
If you can't do your job...

127
00:14:00,519 --> 00:14:02,007
I'm kicking you out of the cat herd.

128
00:14:02,087 --> 00:14:03,463
Now, make him go to sleep!

129
00:14:07,655 --> 00:14:09,015
Feeling a bit drowsy?

130
00:14:09,095 --> 00:14:11,319
Annoying noisy cat.

131
00:14:11,399 --> 00:14:12,439
Not a little bit?

132
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:14,743
Another star just disappeared!

133
00:14:14,823 --> 00:14:17,335
Come on. Just concentrate on the meows.

134
00:14:17,415 --> 00:14:19,191
You need to be closer.

135
00:14:19,271 --> 00:14:20,599
But why do you want me asleep?

136
00:14:20,679 --> 00:14:22,263
Because children, when they're awake...

137
00:14:22,343 --> 00:14:25,143
are noisy, irritating,
troublesome, distracting...

138
00:14:25,223 --> 00:14:28,695
unpredictable, quarrelsome,
naughty nuisances...

139
00:14:28,775 --> 00:14:32,247
but sleeping children are...

140
00:14:32,327 --> 00:14:33,687
perfect.

141
00:14:33,767 --> 00:14:35,735
Whatever. I have to see Moka.

142
00:14:35,815 --> 00:14:39,303
There's more than one way
to make a child go to sl...

143
00:14:40,135 --> 00:14:41,703
I'm sorry.

144
00:14:48,359 --> 00:14:50,327
This kid is gonna drive me...

145
00:14:50,407 --> 00:14:52,983
if I take you to Moka headquarters...

146
00:14:53,063 --> 00:14:54,840
will you go to sleep then?

147
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:56,535
OK.

148
00:14:56,615 --> 00:14:59,015
Well, hang on.

149
00:15:21,895 --> 00:15:23,479
You're gonna wake the whole city up.

150
00:15:23,559 --> 00:15:24,600
Stop shouting!

151
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:26,279
And stop digging in your nails.

152
00:15:28,359 --> 00:15:29,735
Kids.

153
00:16:28,519 --> 00:16:31,015
Here we are, Nocturna headquarters.

154
00:16:32,807 --> 00:16:34,023
Ouch!

155
00:16:34,951 --> 00:16:36,695
Can't you wait just one minute?

156
00:16:36,775 --> 00:16:38,295
We've got to hurry!

157
00:16:38,375 --> 00:16:39,703
We need to talk with Moka.

158
00:16:39,783 --> 00:16:41,367
Take it easy, kid.

159
00:16:41,447 --> 00:16:42,551
You all wait here.

160
00:16:42,631 --> 00:16:44,215
That goes for you, too, Tobermory.

161
00:16:44,295 --> 00:16:46,951
It's time you started behaving properly!

162
00:16:48,167 --> 00:16:50,023
You just stay put, right behind me.

163
00:16:50,151 --> 00:16:51,639
An hour late!

164
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:54,295
Hey, Grandpa,
keep your hair on. It's only...

165
00:16:54,375 --> 00:16:56,855
Mr. Grandpa to you, young man.

166
00:16:56,935 --> 00:16:59,799
Moka is waiting. Impatiently!

167
00:16:59,879 --> 00:17:01,783
Take it up to his office, now!

168
00:17:01,863 --> 00:17:03,447
Do we have to give it to Moka?

169
00:17:03,527 --> 00:17:04,727
I mean, the last time...

170
00:17:04,807 --> 00:17:06,295
he almost bit our heads off.

171
00:17:06,375 --> 00:17:08,023
Well, learn to be punctual...

172
00:17:08,103 --> 00:17:09,655
and that won't happen!

173
00:17:09,735 --> 00:17:12,120
Whatever, Grandpa. Take it easy.

174
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,847
The delivery note.

175
00:17:13,927 --> 00:17:16,759
Sign the delivery note!

176
00:17:16,839 --> 00:17:18,599
Little troublemakers!

177
00:17:20,391 --> 00:17:23,735
What brings you here so... so early?

178
00:17:23,815 --> 00:17:26,007
Well, the kid wants to see Moka...

179
00:17:26,087 --> 00:17:28,247
and I can't get it into his thick skull...

180
00:17:28,327 --> 00:17:29,463
that Moka will see no one.

181
00:17:29,543 --> 00:17:31,415
I have to make him go to sleep, but...

182
00:17:31,495 --> 00:17:33,143
What are you talking about?

183
00:17:33,223 --> 00:17:34,759
About this.

184
00:17:36,583 --> 00:17:38,519
But how can...

185
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:40,199
this kid...

186
00:17:41,447 --> 00:17:43,159
Know something?

187
00:17:43,239 --> 00:17:45,079
Maybe I should take it easy, as well.

188
00:17:45,159 --> 00:17:46,967
We work too hard, Grandpa.

189
00:17:47,047 --> 00:17:48,823
I'll ask for a holiday.

190
00:17:48,903 --> 00:17:51,175
Yeah. That's what I'm gonna do.

191
00:17:55,687 --> 00:17:56,871
Wow!

192
00:18:04,839 --> 00:18:06,311
Right away!

193
00:18:16,711 --> 00:18:19,111
Wait! I need to find Moka.

194
00:18:20,199 --> 00:18:22,087
Where is he now?

195
00:18:23,367 --> 00:18:25,799
Where has that brat got to?

196
00:18:28,391 --> 00:18:29,367
Watch out.

197
00:18:29,447 --> 00:18:31,735
Excuse me.
It's my first important document...

198
00:18:31,815 --> 00:18:33,431
and I mustn't be late.

199
00:18:33,511 --> 00:18:34,647
What can I say?

200
00:18:34,727 --> 00:18:36,600
I find the rookies really cute.

201
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:38,455
Oh, look. There's one coming now.

202
00:18:38,535 --> 00:18:39,911
Yoo-hoo!

203
00:18:40,775 --> 00:18:43,511
Oh, isn't that just the cutest thing.

204
00:18:43,591 --> 00:18:45,879
Attention. We need more crickets...

205
00:18:45,959 --> 00:18:47,160
in Sector 3.

206
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:48,311
Come on, guys!

207
00:18:48,391 --> 00:18:49,831
Let's put a bit of rhythm into the night.

208
00:18:51,687 --> 00:18:52,920
I don't know what's up...

209
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,735
but this don't sound
at all like a cricket.

210
00:18:55,815 --> 00:18:57,847
We got a lot of dry grass out there, boys.

211
00:18:57,927 --> 00:19:00,183
You should have gone at 2100 hours.

212
00:19:00,263 --> 00:19:01,079
Cut that out!

213
00:19:01,159 --> 00:19:03,223
Save some for the gardens, guys!

214
00:19:03,303 --> 00:19:04,375
One more for the road.

215
00:19:04,455 --> 00:19:06,327
You sure? This is your second round.

216
00:19:06,407 --> 00:19:08,087
I said refill!

217
00:19:08,167 --> 00:19:09,927
I know my limits.

218
00:19:12,295 --> 00:19:13,975
Dream delivery.

219
00:19:14,055 --> 00:19:16,151
Last call for dream delivery.

220
00:19:16,231 --> 00:19:18,199
"And then, without knowing how...

221
00:19:18,279 --> 00:19:20,055
"you find yourself in the middle...

222
00:19:20,135 --> 00:19:22,455
of the classroom in your underwear."

223
00:19:22,535 --> 00:19:24,151
What sort of a dream is this?

224
00:19:24,231 --> 00:19:26,967
It has no style. The prose is vulgar.

225
00:19:27,047 --> 00:19:28,375
It lacks depth.

226
00:19:28,455 --> 00:19:30,135
Anyway... I'll let it through...

227
00:19:30,215 --> 00:19:31,543
because we have to go to print...

228
00:19:31,623 --> 00:19:33,335
and we're short on material.

229
00:19:33,415 --> 00:19:34,839
Otherwise...

230
00:19:34,919 --> 00:19:36,423
I thought it had appeal.

231
00:19:39,015 --> 00:19:40,151
You're tumblers, not tossers.

232
00:19:40,231 --> 00:19:42,071
You just push them to the very edge...

233
00:19:42,151 --> 00:19:44,375
so that a leg or an arm is hanging off.

234
00:19:44,455 --> 00:19:46,023
Let's try again.

235
00:19:47,975 --> 00:19:49,223
Oops!

236
00:19:53,287 --> 00:19:54,087
Wait!

237
00:19:54,215 --> 00:19:55,559
We're full.

238
00:19:58,439 --> 00:20:01,815
Wait up!
You can't just barge in like this.

239
00:20:01,895 --> 00:20:03,223
It just isn't done.

240
00:20:03,303 --> 00:20:04,503
Besides, the doorman told me...

241
00:20:04,583 --> 00:20:06,615
that Moka is not seeing anyone today.

242
00:20:06,695 --> 00:20:07,863
He's very busy.

243
00:20:07,943 --> 00:20:10,279
He'll see me. My business is important.

244
00:20:11,463 --> 00:20:13,495
Excuse me.
Could you tell me how to find Moka?

245
00:20:13,575 --> 00:20:15,319
Hey, you. Who let you in?

246
00:20:15,399 --> 00:20:16,855
You are unauthorized personnel.

247
00:20:16,935 --> 00:20:18,360
Relax. The boy is not dangerous.

248
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,575
I found him hanging...

249
00:20:19,655 --> 00:20:21,943
Security,
I have an intruder in the building.

250
00:20:22,023 --> 00:20:23,447
Security?

251
00:20:23,527 --> 00:20:24,471
Security!

252
00:20:24,551 --> 00:20:27,671
They told me that
if it hadn't been for me...

253
00:20:27,751 --> 00:20:28,887
There's a security alert.

254
00:20:28,967 --> 00:20:30,679
Unauthorized person on premises.

255
00:20:30,759 --> 00:20:31,959
You stay put.

256
00:20:32,039 --> 00:20:34,839
Why did you call security?
Was it really necessary?

257
00:20:34,919 --> 00:20:36,919
I was just about to take him back.
It's just...

258
00:20:36,999 --> 00:20:39,127
See, that's why I don't like this place.

259
00:20:39,207 --> 00:20:40,471
Come along with us, sir.

260
00:20:40,551 --> 00:20:42,007
But... but I'm not the intruder!

261
00:20:42,087 --> 00:20:44,663
It's that pig-headed little boy who's...

262
00:20:44,743 --> 00:20:46,615
Not again!

263
00:20:46,695 --> 00:20:48,887
Don't let old fatso
here out of your sight.

264
00:20:48,967 --> 00:20:51,175
He might try something.

265
00:21:10,567 --> 00:21:11,815
I ain't going in there.

266
00:21:11,943 --> 00:21:13,080
Moka will go ballistic.

267
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:14,295
Remember the last time?

268
00:21:14,375 --> 00:21:16,055
The longer you take to give it to him...

269
00:21:16,135 --> 00:21:17,207
the worse it will be.

270
00:21:17,287 --> 00:21:18,711
What do you mean, the longer I take?

271
00:21:18,791 --> 00:21:20,055
You're coming with me.

272
00:21:20,135 --> 00:21:20,983
Me?

273
00:21:21,063 --> 00:21:22,583
Why sacrifice two of us?

274
00:21:22,663 --> 00:21:23,671
You go alone.

275
00:21:23,751 --> 00:21:25,079
Excuse me. Could you tell me...

276
00:21:25,159 --> 00:21:26,695
how to find Moka?

277
00:21:32,295 --> 00:21:34,071
Good luck, kid.

278
00:21:34,151 --> 00:21:35,319
Well, it's about time.

279
00:21:35,399 --> 00:21:36,983
The coffee pot is nearly empty.

280
00:21:37,063 --> 00:21:38,103
What?

281
00:21:38,183 --> 00:21:40,631
Just pour the beans in there.

282
00:21:40,711 --> 00:21:41,783
- But I... - Move it!

283
00:21:41,863 --> 00:21:44,583
I haven't had a drop in the last hour.

284
00:22:01,735 --> 00:22:03,000
Are you Moka?

285
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:04,920
The head honcho who runs Nocturna?

286
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,840
Well, well, well. What have we here?

287
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:09,687
A boy. So, tell me, what are you here for?

288
00:22:09,767 --> 00:22:10,775
I have to speak with you.

289
00:22:10,855 --> 00:22:12,087
Speak? No, no, no, no, no.

290
00:22:12,167 --> 00:22:14,407
I'm far too busy, far too busy.

291
00:22:17,671 --> 00:22:19,687
But it's very important!

292
00:22:21,383 --> 00:22:23,287
Let's have a look.

293
00:22:23,367 --> 00:22:25,239
I've got a visit from the union...

294
00:22:25,319 --> 00:22:26,663
a content meeting...

295
00:22:27,527 --> 00:22:29,367
You're in luck. I have a free slot.

296
00:22:29,447 --> 00:22:30,983
Two minutes.

297
00:22:31,783 --> 00:22:33,239
So, are you going to tell me...

298
00:22:33,319 --> 00:22:34,871
or do you prefer to waste
your two minutes?

299
00:22:34,951 --> 00:22:36,695
Night finishes at 6:00, boy.

300
00:22:36,775 --> 00:22:39,063
Well, you see, Mr. Moka...

301
00:22:39,143 --> 00:22:40,631
it's about the stars.

302
00:22:40,711 --> 00:22:42,167
Stars? I thought you'd come...

303
00:22:42,247 --> 00:22:43,383
to report a missing sock...

304
00:22:43,463 --> 00:22:45,207
or complain that your sheets
get tangled up.

305
00:22:45,287 --> 00:22:46,455
Really, it's my star...

306
00:22:46,535 --> 00:22:48,120
but not just my star, because...

307
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,303
You're a little boy.

308
00:22:49,383 --> 00:22:50,743
What have you got to do with the stars?

309
00:22:50,823 --> 00:22:51,895
Shouldn't you be in bed?

310
00:22:51,975 --> 00:22:53,303
But that's the point!

311
00:22:53,383 --> 00:22:55,735
I can't go to sleep
because my star has disappeared...

312
00:22:55,815 --> 00:22:57,527
and I heard that you're the one...

313
00:22:57,607 --> 00:22:58,743
in charge of everything here.

314
00:22:58,823 --> 00:23:00,695
Precisely. It's a big job.

315
00:23:00,775 --> 00:23:02,807
You have no idea...

316
00:23:02,887 --> 00:23:05,207
tangling sheets, placing bits of fluff...

317
00:23:05,287 --> 00:23:06,583
putting sleep in your eyes.

318
00:23:06,663 --> 00:23:08,151
For example, look!

319
00:23:08,231 --> 00:23:09,975
Do you remember ever waking up...

320
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:11,511
without untidy hair?

321
00:23:11,591 --> 00:23:14,231
Or not hearing creaky floorboards
at night?

322
00:23:14,311 --> 00:23:15,927
You have them to thank for all of that,

323
00:23:16,007 --> 00:23:18,231
the loyal, dedicated workers of the night.

324
00:23:18,311 --> 00:23:20,567
Everything has to work
in perfect harmony...

325
00:23:20,647 --> 00:23:21,975
or else it all falls apart...

326
00:23:22,055 --> 00:23:23,511
and then what will you have?

327
00:23:23,591 --> 00:23:24,631
I don't know.

328
00:23:24,711 --> 00:23:26,279
And you don't want to know.

329
00:23:26,375 --> 00:23:27,863
It would give you goose bumps.

330
00:23:27,943 --> 00:23:29,239
That's why it's so important...

331
00:23:29,319 --> 00:23:30,583
about the stars disappearing.

332
00:23:30,663 --> 00:23:32,071
You have to do something.

333
00:23:33,095 --> 00:23:34,135
I have to?

334
00:23:34,215 --> 00:23:36,711
You're telling me what to do?

335
00:23:38,183 --> 00:23:40,183
I'm the grand master supervisor...

336
00:23:40,263 --> 00:23:41,655
and a little boy...

337
00:23:41,735 --> 00:23:43,159
is telling me what to do.

338
00:23:43,239 --> 00:23:44,471
You don't seem to understand.

339
00:23:44,551 --> 00:23:47,927
I have underlings
who take care of little things.

340
00:23:48,007 --> 00:23:50,007
Little things? So you mean...

341
00:23:50,087 --> 00:23:52,375
that there's someone
who's taking care of the stars?

342
00:23:52,455 --> 00:23:54,103
Of course, genius.

343
00:23:54,183 --> 00:23:55,831
The star keeper.

344
00:23:55,911 --> 00:23:57,847
Well, he's not doing a very good job.

345
00:23:57,927 --> 00:24:00,599
He's lost 3 of his stars, probably more...

346
00:24:00,679 --> 00:24:02,903
and I'm the one sounding the alarm!

347
00:24:02,983 --> 00:24:05,367
I give you my valuable time...

348
00:24:05,447 --> 00:24:08,760
and you... you come here and tell me...

349
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:11,543
I don't know how to do my job properly?

350
00:24:11,623 --> 00:24:13,655
Do you see any kids here?

351
00:24:13,735 --> 00:24:17,527
No. Because kids don't solve problems.

352
00:24:17,607 --> 00:24:20,280
Kids only eat chocolate, destroy things...

353
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:21,463
and snivel!

354
00:24:21,543 --> 00:24:23,415
I'm sorry. I didn't...

355
00:24:23,495 --> 00:24:24,951
I didn't mean to, but...

356
00:24:25,031 --> 00:24:26,679
but you only have to look at the sky...

357
00:24:26,759 --> 00:24:27,831
and see for yourself!

358
00:24:27,911 --> 00:24:29,975
Someone has to tell the star keeper.

359
00:24:30,055 --> 00:24:32,567
I'm not going to give him
any notification...

360
00:24:32,647 --> 00:24:34,743
and do you know why?

361
00:24:34,823 --> 00:24:38,295
Because in my night,
there are no mistakes!

362
00:24:38,375 --> 00:24:39,719
But l...

363
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:42,087
You've wasted enough of my time.

364
00:24:51,207 --> 00:24:53,767
Be sure to sign out at the door.

365
00:24:56,743 --> 00:24:59,127
All that coffee can't be good for him.

366
00:24:59,207 --> 00:25:00,999
So now what?

367
00:25:25,415 --> 00:25:27,543
He swallowed the bait, boss.

368
00:25:27,623 --> 00:25:29,271
Excellent work, Pee.

369
00:25:29,351 --> 00:25:30,983
Now we'll just have to wait.

370
00:25:32,519 --> 00:25:34,519
How can they do this to me?

371
00:25:34,599 --> 00:25:36,183
Kicked out of the tower...

372
00:25:36,263 --> 00:25:37,399
how humiliating!

373
00:25:37,479 --> 00:25:39,383
All thanks to you, Tobermory.

374
00:25:39,463 --> 00:25:41,335
Where did I go wrong with you?

375
00:25:41,415 --> 00:25:44,183
Instead of inducing sleep,
you sleep yourself!

376
00:25:44,263 --> 00:25:48,007
And now your boy is on the loose
in Moka's tower.

377
00:25:48,967 --> 00:25:51,015
Why can't you be like the other cats?

378
00:25:56,295 --> 00:25:57,959
Hi, cat shepherd.

379
00:26:02,375 --> 00:26:04,311
There you are! Got kicked out...

380
00:26:04,391 --> 00:26:06,519
before you got to Moka, I suppose?

381
00:26:06,599 --> 00:26:08,455
No. I saw him.

382
00:26:09,511 --> 00:26:10,359
Well, then...

383
00:26:10,439 --> 00:26:12,503
Remember our deal. I take you to Moka...

384
00:26:12,583 --> 00:26:14,455
and then you agree to go to bed.

385
00:26:14,535 --> 00:26:16,343
But I can't!

386
00:26:16,423 --> 00:26:19,191
I have to... do what Moka told me.

387
00:26:19,271 --> 00:26:21,111
And what's that?

388
00:26:21,191 --> 00:26:23,223
To... to find the star keeper...

389
00:26:23,303 --> 00:26:25,687
and tell him about the missing stars.

390
00:26:25,767 --> 00:26:28,663
Moka told you that?

391
00:26:28,743 --> 00:26:30,199
Y-Y-yes.

392
00:26:30,279 --> 00:26:34,151
I think I'll just go up
and ask Moka about this.

393
00:26:34,855 --> 00:26:36,263
That's not a good idea!

394
00:26:37,479 --> 00:26:38,455
Why?

395
00:26:38,535 --> 00:26:41,015
He... he's very busy right now...

396
00:26:41,095 --> 00:26:42,583
and he said that he...

397
00:26:42,663 --> 00:26:44,280
didn't want to be bothered.

398
00:26:44,360 --> 00:26:45,975
Oh, don't worry about that.

399
00:26:46,055 --> 00:26:47,095
I can get an appointment.

400
00:26:47,175 --> 00:26:48,951
But... but look what he gave me,

401
00:26:49,031 --> 00:26:51,207
the star keeper's address.

402
00:26:52,295 --> 00:26:53,847
What's that you have there?

403
00:26:53,927 --> 00:26:55,639
What do you know?

404
00:26:55,719 --> 00:26:56,727
An official file.

405
00:26:56,807 --> 00:26:58,423
It's true, after all.

406
00:26:58,503 --> 00:26:59,895
He is at the lighthouse.

407
00:26:59,975 --> 00:27:01,623
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

408
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:03,447
Have you any idea how far that is?

409
00:27:03,527 --> 00:27:05,495
It'd take you all night to get there...

410
00:27:05,575 --> 00:27:06,775
and that means...

411
00:27:06,855 --> 00:27:08,759
I can't afford a blot like
that on my record.

412
00:27:08,839 --> 00:27:12,087
OK.
I'll take you to see the star keeper...

413
00:27:12,167 --> 00:27:14,711
but afterwards, you go straight to bed.

414
00:27:14,791 --> 00:27:16,247
After all, I've only got...

415
00:27:16,327 --> 00:27:17,880
one job left to do tonight.

416
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:18,999
What?

417
00:27:19,079 --> 00:27:20,455
I have to put you to sleep.

418
00:27:21,415 --> 00:27:23,799
So let's hurry. The night ends at 6 AM.

419
00:27:23,879 --> 00:27:26,023
There's no time to waste.

420
00:27:53,095 --> 00:27:54,807
"You try to cover yourself
as best you can...

421
00:27:54,887 --> 00:27:57,463
"but the other children keep
on laughing at you...

422
00:27:57,543 --> 00:27:58,887
while the teacher..."

423
00:27:59,687 --> 00:28:02,503
The dreams they write these days.

424
00:28:12,743 --> 00:28:14,727
Really good quality.

425
00:28:25,319 --> 00:28:27,415
Wow! What a lot of cats.

426
00:28:27,495 --> 00:28:29,767
Are they going to follow us all the way?

427
00:28:30,695 --> 00:28:32,760
That shows what you know.

428
00:28:32,840 --> 00:28:34,999
Every cat is assigned a child...

429
00:28:35,079 --> 00:28:36,887
to watch over during the night...

430
00:28:36,967 --> 00:28:40,407
and take care of their sleeping
with their meowing.

431
00:28:40,487 --> 00:28:42,759
It's a great responsibility.

432
00:28:43,527 --> 00:28:45,783
So, mine is Tobermory?

433
00:28:45,863 --> 00:28:48,663
Yeah.
A comatose cat for an insomniac infant.

434
00:28:48,743 --> 00:28:50,375
Perfect match.

435
00:28:57,223 --> 00:28:58,487
Look at it.

436
00:28:58,567 --> 00:28:59,991
Isn't it beautiful?

437
00:29:00,071 --> 00:29:01,815
I don't really like the night.

438
00:29:01,895 --> 00:29:04,471
What? You can't mean that!

439
00:29:04,551 --> 00:29:07,127
It's dark and spooky and depressing.

440
00:29:07,207 --> 00:29:08,727
I don't enjoy it at all.

441
00:29:08,807 --> 00:29:10,583
But it's full of wonderful things!

442
00:29:10,663 --> 00:29:12,759
The only good things
about the night are the stars...

443
00:29:12,839 --> 00:29:14,871
and now they're disappearing.

444
00:29:14,951 --> 00:29:16,855
Of all the strange, annoying...

445
00:29:16,935 --> 00:29:18,039
barbarous children...

446
00:29:18,119 --> 00:29:21,095
Silence! We're trying to make music here.

447
00:29:22,343 --> 00:29:23,479
What's the matter?

448
00:29:23,559 --> 00:29:24,823
It's a Whisperer.

449
00:29:24,903 --> 00:29:28,375
You think things happen
by accident at night?

450
00:29:28,455 --> 00:29:30,151
Pay attention.

451
00:30:24,807 --> 00:30:26,407
Wow.

452
00:30:45,063 --> 00:30:46,567
So unprofessional!

453
00:31:07,431 --> 00:31:09,751
What the... I don't believe it!

454
00:31:09,831 --> 00:31:11,383
What? What is it?

455
00:31:11,463 --> 00:31:13,303
The cat shepherd is with Tim.

456
00:31:13,383 --> 00:31:15,223
What the devil are they doing together?

457
00:31:15,303 --> 00:31:17,079
This is not part of the plan.

458
00:31:17,159 --> 00:31:18,455
It could ruin everything!

459
00:31:18,535 --> 00:31:21,591
Get the cat shepherd away immediately!

460
00:31:21,671 --> 00:31:25,015
Boss! Do you want me to do... that?

461
00:31:25,095 --> 00:31:26,423
That?

462
00:31:26,503 --> 00:31:28,119
Don't even think about it.

463
00:31:28,199 --> 00:31:31,383
There's no need for us
to go to such extremes.

464
00:31:31,463 --> 00:31:33,719
OK, OK. I'll be there...

465
00:31:33,799 --> 00:31:37,255
faster than you can say "Psss..."

466
00:31:39,431 --> 00:31:40,503
Wasn't bad.

467
00:31:40,583 --> 00:31:41,687
Pretty good.

468
00:31:41,767 --> 00:31:42,840
I'm exhausted.

469
00:31:42,920 --> 00:31:44,055
See you, Jimmy.

470
00:31:44,135 --> 00:31:46,487
You were terrific today. Well done.

471
00:31:46,567 --> 00:31:49,095
Well done for a beginner.

472
00:31:53,480 --> 00:31:54,551
How insensitive!

473
00:31:54,631 --> 00:31:57,495
Falling asleep at one of my best concerts.

474
00:31:57,575 --> 00:31:59,751
Wake up, you mangy beast!

475
00:32:05,063 --> 00:32:06,935
Now what do you have to say
about the night?

476
00:32:07,015 --> 00:32:09,335
Still think it's depressing?

477
00:32:09,415 --> 00:32:10,327
What I will say...

478
00:32:10,407 --> 00:32:13,303
is that it's getting darker all the time.

479
00:32:13,383 --> 00:32:14,711
We have to hurry!

480
00:32:14,791 --> 00:32:15,799
Of course, of course.

481
00:32:15,879 --> 00:32:17,575
Come on, guys, let's move it.

482
00:32:20,263 --> 00:32:22,071
Where are you all going?

483
00:32:22,151 --> 00:32:23,671
What's wrong?

484
00:32:23,751 --> 00:32:26,215
Why are you all leaving the pack?

485
00:32:28,903 --> 00:32:30,503
What is it?

486
00:32:36,423 --> 00:32:37,831
What are you looking at?

487
00:32:45,607 --> 00:32:48,455
What is that... thing?

488
00:32:49,991 --> 00:32:52,743
I don't know.

489
00:32:56,583 --> 00:32:57,623
No!

490
00:32:57,703 --> 00:32:58,711
What?

491
00:32:58,791 --> 00:33:00,375
It's too dark in here.

492
00:33:00,455 --> 00:33:02,423
I need to be where there's light.

493
00:33:02,503 --> 00:33:03,671
Please!

494
00:33:03,751 --> 00:33:06,199
All right, all right. Calm down.

495
00:33:06,279 --> 00:33:07,415
Look, over there.

496
00:33:07,495 --> 00:33:09,607
There's a place.

497
00:33:12,423 --> 00:33:14,903
You'll be OK here. Wait for me.

498
00:33:14,983 --> 00:33:16,183
- But... - Take it easy.

499
00:33:16,263 --> 00:33:18,295
I'm only going to tail the pack.

500
00:33:18,375 --> 00:33:20,887
Tobermory will stay with you. OK?

501
00:33:20,967 --> 00:33:22,535
I'll just be a second, then.

502
00:33:38,343 --> 00:33:40,199
Thanks, Tobermory.

503
00:33:45,575 --> 00:33:46,839
Oh, hideous! Look at it.

504
00:33:46,919 --> 00:33:48,887
Not one tangled strand!

505
00:33:48,967 --> 00:33:51,303
She must have brushed it 100 times.

506
00:33:54,440 --> 00:33:55,543
Well, what can we do?

507
00:33:55,623 --> 00:33:56,887
Well, I was thinking...

508
00:33:56,967 --> 00:33:58,839
sort of a prehistoric style.

509
00:33:58,919 --> 00:34:01,367
Clumps. I'm seeing clumps.

510
00:34:01,447 --> 00:34:03,031
It's a challenge, girls...

511
00:34:03,111 --> 00:34:04,791
but I know we're up to it.

512
00:34:04,871 --> 00:34:06,599
Now let's get to work!

513
00:34:10,503 --> 00:34:11,543
Oh, no.

514
00:34:11,623 --> 00:34:13,239
No. Too conventional.

515
00:34:13,319 --> 00:34:15,191
No. No. No personality.

516
00:34:15,271 --> 00:34:17,863
More clumps. More clumps!

517
00:34:20,423 --> 00:34:23,383
Now, now, now... Now it lacks allure.

518
00:34:23,463 --> 00:34:24,919
That's not like us!

519
00:34:24,999 --> 00:34:26,695
I told you... clumps.

520
00:34:30,855 --> 00:34:32,119
Now, that's classy!

521
00:34:32,199 --> 00:34:34,711
Now, girls, we've outdone ourselves.

522
00:34:34,791 --> 00:34:36,775
Clumps always work.

523
00:34:38,567 --> 00:34:41,111
- A boy. - And he's awake!

524
00:34:41,191 --> 00:34:43,479
He's seen too much.

525
00:34:43,559 --> 00:34:45,207
Hey! Tobermory, help!

526
00:34:45,287 --> 00:34:46,663
Look at that.

527
00:34:48,519 --> 00:34:50,807
We have to do something about it.

528
00:34:50,887 --> 00:34:52,519
No question.

529
00:34:59,463 --> 00:35:01,047
Be on the lookout, guys...

530
00:35:01,127 --> 00:35:02,999
and try to stay out of trouble.

531
00:35:03,079 --> 00:35:05,367
Strange things are happening tonight.

532
00:35:05,447 --> 00:35:07,623
I'm counting on you.

533
00:35:13,063 --> 00:35:15,000
We can't concentrate.

534
00:35:15,080 --> 00:35:16,599
You're tickling me.

535
00:35:16,679 --> 00:35:18,007
If you keep still...

536
00:35:18,087 --> 00:35:19,447
we'll turn you into...

537
00:35:19,527 --> 00:35:21,255
a work of art on legs!

538
00:35:22,279 --> 00:35:24,343
There's no time for art tonight.

539
00:35:24,423 --> 00:35:26,007
We've got an important mission.

540
00:35:26,087 --> 00:35:27,095
Come on, Tim.

541
00:35:27,175 --> 00:35:29,015
But he's in our work area!

542
00:35:29,095 --> 00:35:30,327
He belongs to us!

543
00:35:30,407 --> 00:35:32,183
He's destined to be our...

544
00:35:32,263 --> 00:35:33,847
Oh, God, spit it out!

545
00:35:33,927 --> 00:35:35,639
Our masterpiece.

546
00:35:35,719 --> 00:35:38,679
They think I should change my look.

547
00:35:38,759 --> 00:35:39,799
Not tonight.

548
00:35:39,879 --> 00:35:41,015
Sorry.

549
00:35:41,095 --> 00:35:43,367
Well, maybe we'll see each other again.

550
00:35:44,135 --> 00:35:46,647
Someday we'll find him, girls.

551
00:35:46,727 --> 00:35:47,959
We will.

552
00:35:48,039 --> 00:35:48,855
And then?

553
00:35:48,935 --> 00:35:51,335
We'll work wonders with that curl.

554
00:35:59,271 --> 00:36:01,527
Shepherd, what was that?

555
00:36:01,607 --> 00:36:02,519
The hair messers.

556
00:36:02,599 --> 00:36:04,023
They drive me up the wall sometimes.

557
00:36:04,103 --> 00:36:05,559
You know what I'm talking about.

558
00:36:05,639 --> 00:36:08,919
I know. But I'm sure
it has nothing to do with Nocturna.

559
00:36:08,999 --> 00:36:10,647
Do you think we're in danger?

560
00:36:10,727 --> 00:36:13,239
Danger?
Moka makes sure things are in order.

561
00:36:13,319 --> 00:36:14,520
We needn't worry.

562
00:36:14,600 --> 00:36:16,583
Of course. Moka.

563
00:36:20,167 --> 00:36:22,200
There they are!

564
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:24,055
All right, my little ones.

565
00:36:24,135 --> 00:36:25,751
You know what you have to do.

566
00:36:25,831 --> 00:36:29,447
Go! Quickly!
And make your Uncle Pee proud of you!

567
00:36:37,959 --> 00:36:39,607
How can you see where you're going?

568
00:36:39,687 --> 00:36:41,015
You're always worrying.

569
00:36:41,095 --> 00:36:43,575
I could get round Nocturna
with my eyes closed.

570
00:36:43,655 --> 00:36:46,727
Just wonder
why there's so much fog tonight.

571
00:36:49,735 --> 00:36:51,111
Look out!

572
00:37:13,127 --> 00:37:15,399
Tobermory, are you all right?

573
00:37:18,503 --> 00:37:19,959
Cat shepherd?

574
00:37:20,039 --> 00:37:22,471
Cat shepherd?

575
00:37:30,983 --> 00:37:33,127
Uh, hello?

576
00:37:47,463 --> 00:37:48,503
It's...

577
00:37:48,583 --> 00:37:50,247
It's a star!

578
00:37:53,031 --> 00:37:55,927
Stop! Wait. I'm not gonna hurt you.

579
00:37:56,007 --> 00:37:58,007
I got him!

580
00:37:58,087 --> 00:38:00,151
It's the kidnapper!

581
00:38:00,231 --> 00:38:01,847
Get him before he gets away!

582
00:38:01,927 --> 00:38:03,767
Kid... napper. Kidnapper.

583
00:38:03,847 --> 00:38:05,655
Kidnapper! Kidnapper!

584
00:38:05,735 --> 00:38:07,319
I'm not the...

585
00:38:07,399 --> 00:38:08,727
We got you!

586
00:38:08,807 --> 00:38:11,959
Kidnapper! Kidnapper!

587
00:38:12,039 --> 00:38:13,495
You won't get away this time.

588
00:38:13,575 --> 00:38:14,551
We got you surrounded.

589
00:38:14,631 --> 00:38:16,247
Star! What's going on?

590
00:38:16,327 --> 00:38:19,127
Star? Who are you calling a star,

591
00:38:19,207 --> 00:38:20,535
you little punk?

592
00:38:20,615 --> 00:38:23,335
I'll show you who's a star!

593
00:38:25,767 --> 00:38:26,935
Nooo!

594
00:38:27,015 --> 00:38:29,559
Stop him! Stop that kid!

595
00:38:29,639 --> 00:38:31,591
Murray! After him!

596
00:38:32,903 --> 00:38:34,359
Don't let him get away!

597
00:38:34,439 --> 00:38:35,815
After him!

598
00:38:42,407 --> 00:38:44,215
What happened?

599
00:38:44,295 --> 00:38:45,783
The boy!

600
00:38:45,863 --> 00:38:47,287
Tim!

601
00:38:47,367 --> 00:38:49,319
Where are you?

602
00:38:53,031 --> 00:38:54,983
Focus.

603
00:39:05,671 --> 00:39:07,287
Wait for me, guys.

604
00:39:07,367 --> 00:39:09,543
Party time!

605
00:39:56,327 --> 00:39:57,623
Stop there.

606
00:39:57,703 --> 00:39:59,847
You're not gonna have your way.

607
00:40:05,063 --> 00:40:07,047
Just a minute.

608
00:40:12,775 --> 00:40:14,695
I said don't move!

609
00:40:23,623 --> 00:40:26,343
Good cat. Shame the shepherd's not here.

610
00:40:33,575 --> 00:40:35,239
A melon?

611
00:40:40,551 --> 00:40:42,727
There he is, boys!

612
00:40:44,167 --> 00:40:46,807
Kidnapper! Kidnapper!

613
00:40:46,887 --> 00:40:48,951
Kidnapper!

614
00:40:49,031 --> 00:40:50,807
The kidnapper!

615
00:40:50,887 --> 00:40:52,279
Pulverize him!

616
00:40:52,359 --> 00:40:53,847
I didn't mean it. I...

617
00:40:53,927 --> 00:40:55,495
Broke his filament!

618
00:40:56,807 --> 00:40:58,199
For Murray!

619
00:40:58,279 --> 00:41:00,311
Get off me!

620
00:41:00,391 --> 00:41:02,887
Foggers, clear this fog!

621
00:41:09,703 --> 00:41:12,023
Cat shepherd! You came back for me!

622
00:41:12,103 --> 00:41:13,367
Well, I can't have you

623
00:41:13,447 --> 00:41:15,159
wandering around awake all night, can I?

624
00:41:15,239 --> 00:41:16,791
Looks bad on my record.

625
00:41:16,871 --> 00:41:18,615
It's not the kidnapper.

626
00:41:18,695 --> 00:41:20,087
It's the big guy!

627
00:41:20,167 --> 00:41:21,815
Now, tell me, what's going on?

628
00:41:21,895 --> 00:41:23,127
Why are you chasing this boy here?

629
00:41:23,207 --> 00:41:24,887
We thought he was the kidnapper.

630
00:41:24,967 --> 00:41:27,671
Kidnapper. Kidnapper. Kidnapper.

631
00:41:27,751 --> 00:41:30,135
So many of us in the gang

632
00:41:30,215 --> 00:41:31,831
have disappeared without a trace!

633
00:41:31,911 --> 00:41:34,519
That's why Murray offered to be bait,

634
00:41:34,599 --> 00:41:36,791
to catch the kidnapper red-handed.

635
00:41:36,871 --> 00:41:39,351
And he'd do it again.

636
00:41:39,431 --> 00:41:42,583
Takes more than a little crack
to burn me out.

637
00:41:42,663 --> 00:41:44,695
Murray! Hooray!

638
00:41:44,775 --> 00:41:46,487
Hey, get back, get back.

639
00:41:46,567 --> 00:41:48,055
Don't crowd the champ.

640
00:41:48,135 --> 00:41:49,015
Murray!

641
00:41:49,095 --> 00:41:51,127
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to drop you.

642
00:41:51,207 --> 00:41:52,471
I thought you were a star

643
00:41:52,551 --> 00:41:54,135
that had fallen from the sky.

644
00:41:54,215 --> 00:41:55,831
Hehe, hey,

645
00:41:55,911 --> 00:41:57,399
Easy mistake.

646
00:41:57,479 --> 00:42:00,695
We're luminouses
who usually hang around lampposts...

647
00:42:00,775 --> 00:42:01,751
and on stoplights...

648
00:42:01,831 --> 00:42:04,535
but things have been getting
so hot for us...

649
00:42:04,615 --> 00:42:06,119
we had to go on the run.

650
00:42:06,215 --> 00:42:08,279
So you mean luminouses
have been disappearing

651
00:42:08,359 --> 00:42:09,623
along with stars.

652
00:42:09,703 --> 00:42:12,487
Yeah. We're losing our spark.

653
00:42:14,503 --> 00:42:16,343
I don't find that funny.

654
00:42:16,423 --> 00:42:17,463
Sorry, champ.

655
00:42:17,543 --> 00:42:19,607
I could have sworn he was the kidnapper.

656
00:42:19,687 --> 00:42:21,367
But you say he's not the one.

657
00:42:21,447 --> 00:42:23,575
Moka sent the boy to find out
what's happening.

658
00:42:23,655 --> 00:42:25,783
That's why we can't stay.
We have to move on.

659
00:42:25,863 --> 00:42:26,903
Good luck.

660
00:42:26,983 --> 00:42:28,407
Sorry about cracking you.

661
00:42:28,487 --> 00:42:29,847
No problem!

662
00:42:29,927 --> 00:42:31,191
My mother always said...

663
00:42:31,271 --> 00:42:33,367
I was a little cracked, anyway.

664
00:42:33,447 --> 00:42:34,999
Bye, guys!

665
00:42:35,079 --> 00:42:36,535
See you later! See you!

666
00:42:36,615 --> 00:42:39,271
I said... just a minute!

667
00:42:41,927 --> 00:42:44,375
This is the night report.
We're snowed under.

668
00:42:44,455 --> 00:42:46,903
Half the city is in darkness,
and nobody knows why.

669
00:42:46,983 --> 00:42:48,535
There have been complaints
from the unions...

670
00:42:48,615 --> 00:42:51,063
an increase in accidents
through lack of visibility...

671
00:42:51,143 --> 00:42:52,247
streets aren't safe...

672
00:42:52,327 --> 00:42:53,847
the crickets are about to call a strike...

673
00:42:53,927 --> 00:42:55,927
and the knock-downers have simply...

674
00:42:56,007 --> 00:42:57,895
stopped knocking down.

675
00:42:59,335 --> 00:43:01,655
Forgive me, Sir, but people are asking...

676
00:43:01,735 --> 00:43:03,671
a lot of questions about...

677
00:43:03,751 --> 00:43:05,815
about the light, and...

678
00:43:05,895 --> 00:43:07,655
that shadow.

679
00:43:10,919 --> 00:43:12,023
I'm sorry!

680
00:43:12,103 --> 00:43:13,623
Questions, questions.

681
00:43:13,703 --> 00:43:16,231
And who's gonna answer my questions?

682
00:43:17,063 --> 00:43:18,359
Ta-da! Here I am.

683
00:43:18,439 --> 00:43:19,255
Well?

684
00:43:19,335 --> 00:43:21,271
Finito, boss. Precision job.

685
00:43:21,351 --> 00:43:23,127
That is...

686
00:43:23,207 --> 00:43:24,631
just marvelous!

687
00:43:24,711 --> 00:43:26,039
Couldn't be better.

688
00:43:26,119 --> 00:43:29,111
Guess who's very shortly going
to have a...

689
00:43:29,191 --> 00:43:31,703
Raise? A raise, boss?

690
00:43:31,783 --> 00:43:32,823
A problem!

691
00:43:32,903 --> 00:43:33,911
What?

692
00:43:33,991 --> 00:43:35,399
He's still with the shepherd.

693
00:43:36,679 --> 00:43:37,879
How did he do that?

694
00:43:37,959 --> 00:43:39,991
I never dreamed I'd have to do this.

695
00:43:40,071 --> 00:43:43,159
The time has come for you to do it.

696
00:43:43,239 --> 00:43:45,687
Do you really mean... that?

697
00:43:45,767 --> 00:43:47,447
Yes.

698
00:43:47,527 --> 00:43:50,551
And remember, if you mess up...

699
00:43:50,631 --> 00:43:53,095
it could be too late.

700
00:44:02,087 --> 00:44:04,295
Enough for today.

701
00:44:07,367 --> 00:44:09,255
Down you go, boys.

702
00:44:26,855 --> 00:44:29,351
The port is just over there.

703
00:44:31,751 --> 00:44:34,407
We'll soon reach the lighthouse.

704
00:44:35,335 --> 00:44:37,495
Look how many stars and streetlights...

705
00:44:37,575 --> 00:44:39,127
have disappeared now.

706
00:44:39,207 --> 00:44:40,440
It's getting so dark!

707
00:44:40,520 --> 00:44:42,391
You were right. Something is happening.

708
00:44:42,471 --> 00:44:44,375
I'm sorry I didn't believe you.

709
00:44:44,455 --> 00:44:46,391
What if all the stars go out?

710
00:44:46,471 --> 00:44:48,087
That can't happen.

711
00:44:48,167 --> 00:44:49,367
It's impossible.

712
00:44:49,447 --> 00:44:51,031
If there were no stars...

713
00:44:51,111 --> 00:44:52,663
Then what?

714
00:44:52,743 --> 00:44:53,880
Then... l guess...

715
00:44:53,960 --> 00:44:55,607
that Nocturna would disappear.

716
00:44:55,687 --> 00:44:58,615
And what about you and your cats?

717
00:44:58,695 --> 00:45:00,631
Moka and the hair messers?

718
00:45:00,711 --> 00:45:02,199
We're all part of Nocturna.

719
00:45:02,279 --> 00:45:05,239
But... you can't just disappear like that.

720
00:45:05,319 --> 00:45:07,383
I don't want to be on my own again.

721
00:45:07,463 --> 00:45:09,783
What's this? You're worrying about us now?

722
00:45:09,863 --> 00:45:12,023
I thought you didn't like the night.

723
00:45:12,103 --> 00:45:15,319
Anyway, I promise I won't disappear,

724
00:45:15,399 --> 00:45:18,631
not while there are awkward children
who won't go to bed.

725
00:45:21,735 --> 00:45:23,191
Take it easy.

726
00:45:23,271 --> 00:45:25,527
We'll get the stars back
to their proper place.

727
00:45:25,607 --> 00:45:27,511
They seem to be important to you.

728
00:45:27,591 --> 00:45:29,751
Of course they are! Mama told me...

729
00:45:29,831 --> 00:45:32,119
that every person has a star.

730
00:45:32,199 --> 00:45:33,687
You choose one, and then you...

731
00:45:33,767 --> 00:45:35,319
just have to look up at the sky...

732
00:45:35,399 --> 00:45:37,463
and see its light.

733
00:45:37,543 --> 00:45:39,351
You're never alone at night...

734
00:45:39,431 --> 00:45:41,303
because your star is with you...

735
00:45:41,383 --> 00:45:43,927
protecting you from the dark.

736
00:45:44,007 --> 00:45:46,807
She said it would always be there...

737
00:45:46,887 --> 00:45:49,127
but... it's not.

738
00:45:49,767 --> 00:45:50,999
Don't worry.

739
00:45:51,079 --> 00:45:53,687
I won't leave you on your own. I promise.

740
00:45:53,767 --> 00:45:56,087
We'll have the stars shining up there...

741
00:45:56,167 --> 00:45:57,527
before dawn breaks.

742
00:45:57,607 --> 00:45:59,703
After all, we make a good team.

743
00:45:59,783 --> 00:46:01,239
You mean... me and you?

744
00:46:01,319 --> 00:46:03,255
Of course! Look how fast you went...

745
00:46:03,335 --> 00:46:05,271
in front of that gang of luminouses...

746
00:46:05,351 --> 00:46:07,447
and how I stopped them in their tracks.

747
00:46:07,527 --> 00:46:08,903
Right, Tobermory?

748
00:46:09,831 --> 00:46:11,415
I don't know why I bother.

749
00:46:11,495 --> 00:46:13,031
It's pointless.

750
00:46:23,175 --> 00:46:24,551
Got you!

751
00:47:04,615 --> 00:47:06,823
Hold on, shepherd!

752
00:47:18,375 --> 00:47:20,295
Shepherd!

753
00:47:29,287 --> 00:47:31,255
Thanks for coming after me.

754
00:47:31,335 --> 00:47:33,847
Well, we're a team, aren't we?

755
00:47:33,927 --> 00:47:35,543
Yes, I guess.

756
00:47:35,623 --> 00:47:37,255
Sort of.

757
00:48:22,375 --> 00:48:25,383
Peed in the bed again!

758
00:48:51,655 --> 00:48:53,671
It's this way.

759
00:49:05,415 --> 00:49:06,551
It's here.

760
00:49:06,631 --> 00:49:08,567
The gangway joins the pier
to the lighthouse.

761
00:49:08,647 --> 00:49:10,200
We'll be there in a snap.

762
00:49:10,280 --> 00:49:11,575
So we made it.

763
00:49:11,655 --> 00:49:12,471
Almost, mate.

764
00:49:12,551 --> 00:49:13,975
I'm beginning to understand...

765
00:49:14,055 --> 00:49:15,863
why Moka picked you for this mission.

766
00:49:15,943 --> 00:49:18,199
I'm sorry I didn't believe you.

767
00:49:18,279 --> 00:49:19,191
Well...

768
00:49:19,271 --> 00:49:22,215
Shepherd, I just wanted to say...

769
00:49:23,687 --> 00:49:25,415
What is it?

770
00:49:27,239 --> 00:49:28,855
Not again.

771
00:49:28,935 --> 00:49:30,247
Please.

772
00:49:37,191 --> 00:49:38,599
It's your cat pack!

773
00:49:39,303 --> 00:49:40,759
What are you doing?

774
00:49:40,839 --> 00:49:41,943
You should be in the city.

775
00:49:42,023 --> 00:49:43,607
I told you it was dangerous.

776
00:49:43,687 --> 00:49:45,079
Why have you followed us?

777
00:49:45,159 --> 00:49:48,055
Why are you so nervous?
Try to calm down, guys.

778
00:49:48,135 --> 00:49:49,319
Calm down!

779
00:49:50,631 --> 00:49:52,615
Stop!

780
00:49:57,383 --> 00:50:00,439
It's... it's children!

781
00:50:00,519 --> 00:50:01,799
Crying!

782
00:50:04,135 --> 00:50:06,135
They're all awake!

783
00:50:06,215 --> 00:50:09,047
That's why the cats came looking for us.

784
00:50:09,127 --> 00:50:10,647
But how?

785
00:50:10,727 --> 00:50:12,983
It can't be. Every child is awake!

786
00:50:13,063 --> 00:50:15,191
I don't know what's happening.
I have to go back.

787
00:50:15,271 --> 00:50:16,375
You're going?

788
00:50:16,455 --> 00:50:17,495
It's not normal!

789
00:50:17,575 --> 00:50:18,967
I have to sort out this disaster.

790
00:50:19,047 --> 00:50:21,847
But you can't leave me now.
We're really close.

791
00:50:21,927 --> 00:50:24,023
Don't you understand?
I've got a job to do.

792
00:50:24,103 --> 00:50:26,199
What will Moka think if I wander off...

793
00:50:26,279 --> 00:50:28,087
and let every child stay awake all night?

794
00:50:28,167 --> 00:50:30,071
You're only concerned about your job...

795
00:50:30,151 --> 00:50:31,959
and what that Moka thinks!

796
00:50:32,039 --> 00:50:33,879
He didn't even listen to me...

797
00:50:33,959 --> 00:50:36,247
when I told him about the missing stars.

798
00:50:36,327 --> 00:50:40,023
So... the card.
He didn't give it to you, right?

799
00:50:40,103 --> 00:50:42,551
We're here without his permission.

800
00:50:42,631 --> 00:50:44,567
You lied to me.

801
00:50:44,647 --> 00:50:46,487
You wouldn't listen to me!

802
00:50:46,567 --> 00:50:48,983
You've seen what's happening
with the stars and luminouses...

803
00:50:49,063 --> 00:50:50,231
and that shadow.

804
00:50:50,311 --> 00:50:51,927
We don't know what might happen...

805
00:50:52,007 --> 00:50:53,975
if we don't arrive in time.

806
00:50:54,055 --> 00:50:55,575
Stay here and don't move.

807
00:50:55,655 --> 00:50:56,727
You can't come with me.

808
00:50:56,807 --> 00:50:58,423
You said you wouldn't leave me alone.

809
00:50:58,503 --> 00:51:00,071
That really was a lie!

810
00:51:01,671 --> 00:51:03,543
I'll come for you as soon as I finish...

811
00:51:03,623 --> 00:51:04,887
and this time, I'll take you...

812
00:51:04,967 --> 00:51:06,759
to where you should have stayed.

813
00:51:17,255 --> 00:51:19,575
We're not gonna stay here doing nothing...

814
00:51:19,655 --> 00:51:21,431
while the stars are disappearing.

815
00:51:21,511 --> 00:51:23,319
We don't need him.

816
00:51:23,399 --> 00:51:25,319
We don't need anyone.

817
00:51:48,167 --> 00:51:50,327
You two, in there.

818
00:51:50,407 --> 00:51:52,135
The rest of you, follow me!

819
00:51:56,519 --> 00:51:58,295
There's no time to waste.

820
00:51:58,375 --> 00:52:00,120
You, over there, on that balcony.

821
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:01,607
Hurry!

822
00:52:18,247 --> 00:52:19,815
Come on, Tobermory.

823
00:52:21,351 --> 00:52:23,623
Don't be so lazy!

824
00:52:41,927 --> 00:52:43,751
Looks empty.

825
00:52:44,839 --> 00:52:46,647
Star keeper?

826
00:52:46,727 --> 00:52:48,663
Star keeper.

827
00:52:48,743 --> 00:52:50,215
Star keeper!

828
00:53:18,759 --> 00:53:20,823
You're not going to believe this...

829
00:53:20,903 --> 00:53:23,607
but I think I just saw someone up there.

830
00:53:23,687 --> 00:53:26,023
Sure! Sure, Ted.

831
00:53:36,519 --> 00:53:38,679
Now, you two, stay where you belong.

832
00:53:38,759 --> 00:53:41,991
I think everything is under control now.

833
00:53:46,727 --> 00:53:48,183
What are you doing there, girls?

834
00:53:48,263 --> 00:53:49,111
Got a problem?

835
00:53:49,191 --> 00:53:51,255
A problem? We haven't been able...

836
00:53:51,335 --> 00:53:52,823
to undo anyone's hair in peace!

837
00:53:52,903 --> 00:53:54,999
All the children have gone crazy!

838
00:53:55,079 --> 00:53:56,535
On account of that worm.

839
00:53:56,615 --> 00:53:58,359
All right, calm down, calm down.

840
00:53:58,439 --> 00:54:00,087
Who are you talking about?

841
00:54:00,167 --> 00:54:02,359
Who? Who else? Pee!

842
00:54:02,439 --> 00:54:04,920
He's been waking up
all the children in the city!

843
00:54:05,000 --> 00:54:07,800
One day,
I'll wipe that smirk off his face.

844
00:54:07,880 --> 00:54:09,239
Pee? But why?

845
00:54:09,319 --> 00:54:13,415
I think I'm gonna have
to inform Moka about all this.

846
00:54:17,895 --> 00:54:19,415
Star keeper?

847
00:54:19,495 --> 00:54:20,967
Star keeper!

848
00:54:22,407 --> 00:54:24,535
Star keeper!

849
00:54:24,615 --> 00:54:26,135
Who's there?

850
00:54:26,215 --> 00:54:28,471
Someone came. At last!

851
00:54:28,551 --> 00:54:30,551
I was beginning to get a bit frantic.

852
00:54:30,631 --> 00:54:32,760
Wow! You're... You're...

853
00:54:32,840 --> 00:54:34,919
A star.

854
00:54:35,783 --> 00:54:37,879
You're beautiful!

855
00:54:37,959 --> 00:54:38,967
Thank you.

856
00:54:39,047 --> 00:54:41,207
Most people don't see past my position.

857
00:54:41,287 --> 00:54:42,615
What is your position?

858
00:54:42,695 --> 00:54:45,591
Why, I'm the North Star, of course.

859
00:54:45,671 --> 00:54:47,959
Everyone revolves around me.

860
00:54:48,039 --> 00:54:50,263
I'm not bragging. It's literally true.

861
00:54:50,343 --> 00:54:52,247
I know. I see you every night...

862
00:54:52,327 --> 00:54:54,327
and you keep me company...

863
00:54:54,407 --> 00:54:55,575
especially Adhara.

864
00:54:55,655 --> 00:54:57,111
She's my star.

865
00:54:57,191 --> 00:54:58,711
But she suddenly disappeared.

866
00:54:58,791 --> 00:55:01,207
Impossible! Stars don't just disappear.

867
00:55:01,287 --> 00:55:03,415
We've been here for thousands of years.

868
00:55:03,495 --> 00:55:05,303
I think it's a blackout.

869
00:55:05,383 --> 00:55:07,320
We need to use the emergency switches.

870
00:55:07,400 --> 00:55:08,983
The emergency switches?

871
00:55:09,063 --> 00:55:10,775
All stars have one.

872
00:55:10,855 --> 00:55:11,927
Uh! Can't reach it...

873
00:55:12,007 --> 00:55:15,000
but right about there is
my emergency power switch.

874
00:55:15,080 --> 00:55:16,407
See it?

875
00:55:16,487 --> 00:55:18,551
We have to tell the star keeper...

876
00:55:18,631 --> 00:55:19,800
so he can light you all again.

877
00:55:19,880 --> 00:55:21,143
What star keeper?

878
00:55:21,223 --> 00:55:23,703
You know, the one who takes
care of all you stars...

879
00:55:23,783 --> 00:55:25,751
and makes sure
you have everything you need.

880
00:55:25,831 --> 00:55:27,831
I've been around for millennia, kid,

881
00:55:27,911 --> 00:55:30,903
and believe me, men like that don't exist.

882
00:55:30,983 --> 00:55:33,847
But... Then who lives in the lighthouse?

883
00:55:33,927 --> 00:55:34,999
Nobody.

884
00:55:35,079 --> 00:55:37,015
You're the first person I've seen...

885
00:55:37,095 --> 00:55:38,551
in the lighthouse in centuries.

886
00:55:38,631 --> 00:55:41,399
It's all automatic now, you see.

887
00:55:41,479 --> 00:55:43,063
But Moka said...

888
00:55:43,143 --> 00:55:45,383
Then I came all this way for nothing?

889
00:55:46,919 --> 00:55:49,335
Who's gonna save the stars?

890
00:55:49,415 --> 00:55:50,455
What about you?

891
00:55:50,535 --> 00:55:51,575
Me?

892
00:55:51,655 --> 00:55:53,495
You just have to climb up the gangways...

893
00:55:53,575 --> 00:55:55,095
and collect the ones that are not shining.

894
00:55:55,175 --> 00:55:56,663
You can be the star keeper.

895
00:55:56,743 --> 00:55:58,919
You want us to shine again?

896
00:56:59,303 --> 00:57:03,719
Comrades,
we are the last remaining luminouses.

897
00:57:04,199 --> 00:57:08,407
We should stand united
against the enemy...

898
00:57:08,487 --> 00:57:10,855
the kidnapper!

899
00:57:19,207 --> 00:57:21,495
Kidnapper. Kidnapper.

900
00:57:21,575 --> 00:57:23,223
Stupid filament!

901
00:57:23,303 --> 00:57:24,311
Kidnapper!

902
00:57:24,391 --> 00:57:26,087
He's above!

903
00:57:30,055 --> 00:57:31,911
Kidnapper!

904
00:57:43,079 --> 00:57:44,695
I don't understand.

905
00:57:44,775 --> 00:57:47,255
The switch doesn't work. What's wrong?

906
00:57:47,335 --> 00:57:48,919
I don't know!

907
00:57:48,999 --> 00:57:52,279
But if they go any longer
without shining...

908
00:57:52,359 --> 00:57:56,391
that means... they're dead.

909
00:57:58,631 --> 00:57:59,767
No.

910
00:57:59,847 --> 00:58:01,143
No!

911
00:58:01,223 --> 00:58:03,303
That can't happen.

912
00:58:04,775 --> 00:58:06,503
Adhara!

913
00:58:19,400 --> 00:58:21,351
No!

914
00:58:30,599 --> 00:58:32,647
No...

915
00:58:44,423 --> 00:58:46,263
This is an emergency summons to all...

916
00:58:46,343 --> 00:58:49,335
Nocturians, you must come
to the tower immediately.

917
00:58:49,415 --> 00:58:52,471
Immediately! No one must remain outside!

918
00:58:52,551 --> 00:58:54,167
No one!

919
00:58:54,247 --> 00:58:56,151
You must all be very careful!

920
00:58:56,231 --> 00:58:59,207
Protect yourselves from the shadow!

921
00:59:02,823 --> 00:59:05,431
Mr. Moka.
Thank goodness I managed to get here.

922
00:59:05,511 --> 00:59:08,007
We've got to do something. Pee has...

923
00:59:09,095 --> 00:59:10,935
Leave us alone.

924
00:59:11,015 --> 00:59:12,183
We have a lot to talk about.

925
00:59:12,263 --> 00:59:13,495
OK, boss.

926
00:59:13,575 --> 00:59:14,423
Cup of coffee?

927
00:59:14,503 --> 00:59:17,239
I'd rather have an explanation.

928
00:59:17,319 --> 00:59:18,807
Adhara.

929
00:59:18,887 --> 00:59:20,823
You can't leave me alone.

930
00:59:20,903 --> 00:59:22,519
You're my star.

931
00:59:22,599 --> 00:59:24,503
You have to protect me!

932
00:59:24,583 --> 00:59:28,311
You were going to be there forever.

933
00:59:28,391 --> 00:59:30,807
Tim, what are we going to do now?

934
00:59:30,887 --> 00:59:32,759
Moka lied to me.

935
00:59:32,839 --> 00:59:35,607
I have to go back.

936
00:59:35,687 --> 00:59:37,143
Are you sure?

937
00:59:37,223 --> 00:59:38,583
Now I am.

938
00:59:38,663 --> 00:59:42,055
Moka knew everything,
ever since the beginning.

939
00:59:45,511 --> 00:59:47,095
What's that?

940
00:59:47,175 --> 00:59:48,999
What is it?

941
00:59:54,183 --> 00:59:56,999
Quick! Let's get out of here!

942
01:00:00,935 --> 01:00:02,647
It's destroying everything.

943
01:00:02,727 --> 01:00:04,087
It's terrible.

944
01:00:04,167 --> 01:00:05,831
And the shadow is still growing.

945
01:00:05,927 --> 01:00:07,863
It's more dangerous than you can imagine.

946
01:00:07,943 --> 01:00:09,559
Once it puts out the last light...

947
01:00:09,639 --> 01:00:10,743
it will become complete...

948
01:00:10,823 --> 01:00:12,375
and that will be the end of Nocturna!

949
01:00:12,455 --> 01:00:13,591
We've got to stop it!

950
01:00:13,671 --> 01:00:14,775
Stop it? It's too late.

951
01:00:14,855 --> 01:00:15,895
Haven't you realized...

952
01:00:15,975 --> 01:00:17,431
that this has to be done by the boy?

953
01:00:17,511 --> 01:00:19,415
Maybe you're right,
but I have to find him.

954
01:00:19,495 --> 01:00:21,175
I promised I wouldn't leave him alone.

955
01:00:21,255 --> 01:00:22,935
Where do you think you're going?

956
01:00:23,015 --> 01:00:24,855
I won't stay here and do nothing.

957
01:00:24,935 --> 01:00:26,887
That's more your way.

958
01:00:30,727 --> 01:00:32,903
Good luck, then, my friend.

959
01:01:03,495 --> 01:01:07,159
Hey! Big guy!

960
01:01:07,239 --> 01:01:08,215
Over here.

961
01:01:08,295 --> 01:01:10,583
Murray? You're still lit!

962
01:01:10,663 --> 01:01:13,559
Of course. I'm a long-life bulb.

963
01:01:13,639 --> 01:01:15,383
Ain't you going to the meeting?

964
01:01:15,463 --> 01:01:17,015
I can't.
I've got to go and find the boy...

965
01:01:17,095 --> 01:01:18,295
and protect him from the shadow.

966
01:01:18,375 --> 01:01:20,919
Shadow? Hey, please,
you got to take me with you.

967
01:01:20,999 --> 01:01:23,703
I've got some unresolved business
with that slug.

968
01:01:23,783 --> 01:01:25,527
No, my friend. Too dangerous.

969
01:01:25,607 --> 01:01:28,631
Believe me, an angry luminous...

970
01:01:28,711 --> 01:01:32,807
don't know the meaning
of the word "danger."

971
01:01:36,200 --> 01:01:38,391
Look! There's Moka's tower.

972
01:01:38,471 --> 01:01:39,991
You did it!

973
01:01:40,071 --> 01:01:41,911
But how do we get down there?

974
01:01:41,991 --> 01:01:43,399
We can't fly.

975
01:01:44,775 --> 01:01:46,279
Says who?

976
01:01:57,735 --> 01:02:00,583
Did you hear about the stars?

977
01:02:02,503 --> 01:02:03,511
What's going on?

978
01:02:03,591 --> 01:02:06,039
We can't get any work done
without the stars!

979
01:02:06,119 --> 01:02:08,119
There aren't even any luminouses.

980
01:02:08,199 --> 01:02:09,383
What next?

981
01:02:11,015 --> 01:02:12,600
We want an explanation!

982
01:02:12,680 --> 01:02:13,879
We want an explanation!

983
01:02:13,959 --> 01:02:15,671
We want an explanation!

984
01:02:15,751 --> 01:02:18,327
Moka is about to arrive, so quiet down.

985
01:02:18,407 --> 01:02:20,343
How do you expect us to be quiet?

986
01:02:20,423 --> 01:02:22,711
The shadow is destroying
everything in Nocturna!

987
01:02:22,791 --> 01:02:24,887
Moka must tell us what's happening!

988
01:02:24,967 --> 01:02:26,343
Look!

989
01:02:29,415 --> 01:02:32,887
As you know,
we are living through difficult times...

990
01:02:32,967 --> 01:02:36,151
and you want to know
who is causing all this.

991
01:02:36,231 --> 01:02:38,807
You deserve to know who's responsible...

992
01:02:38,887 --> 01:02:41,431
for this devastation, this chaos...

993
01:02:41,511 --> 01:02:43,863
this tragedy.

994
01:02:43,943 --> 01:02:47,160
You demand to know who sent the shadow...

995
01:02:47,240 --> 01:02:49,175
to destroy our night.

996
01:02:49,255 --> 01:02:52,247
And I will tell you.

997
01:02:52,327 --> 01:02:55,639
The person who caused
this is a small boy...

998
01:02:55,719 --> 01:02:57,751
named Tim!

999
01:02:57,831 --> 01:02:59,255
I can't believe it.

1000
01:02:59,335 --> 01:03:00,343
Tim!

1001
01:03:00,423 --> 01:03:01,495
He's a liar.

1002
01:03:01,575 --> 01:03:02,583
The boy?

1003
01:03:02,663 --> 01:03:03,767
It can't be.

1004
01:03:03,847 --> 01:03:06,199
The boy brought the shadow to Nocturna...

1005
01:03:06,279 --> 01:03:10,519
but he's not responsible
for the disaster that confronts us.

1006
01:03:10,599 --> 01:03:14,583
We must never forget
that for some sleepers...

1007
01:03:14,663 --> 01:03:16,311
this is a place to fear,

1008
01:03:16,391 --> 01:03:18,551
nightmares, monsters under the bed...

1009
01:03:18,631 --> 01:03:22,423
nameless things lurking
in dark corners, shadows.

1010
01:03:22,503 --> 01:03:24,151
This is the night for Tim...

1011
01:03:24,231 --> 01:03:26,839
and his fear created this monster...

1012
01:03:26,919 --> 01:03:28,503
which is threatening us...

1013
01:03:28,583 --> 01:03:31,320
putting an end to all traces of light,

1014
01:03:31,400 --> 01:03:33,671
to what he most loves.

1015
01:03:43,847 --> 01:03:46,071
We've got to do something!

1016
01:03:46,151 --> 01:03:47,191
Yeah!

1017
01:03:47,271 --> 01:03:48,311
Do something!

1018
01:03:48,391 --> 01:03:49,399
Do it now!

1019
01:03:49,479 --> 01:03:53,303
No! There was only one way
to defeat the shadow...

1020
01:03:53,383 --> 01:03:56,471
and only one person could do it.

1021
01:03:56,551 --> 01:04:00,279
He had to overcome his fear
by confronting the shadow...

1022
01:04:00,359 --> 01:04:03,991
and he had to find
this courage by himself.

1023
01:04:04,071 --> 01:04:06,215
No one could warn him.

1024
01:04:06,311 --> 01:04:08,471
I tried to make it possible for Tim...

1025
01:04:08,551 --> 01:04:11,543
to make a journey
through Nocturna on his own...

1026
01:04:11,623 --> 01:04:14,359
but I failed, and I'm sorry.

1027
01:04:14,439 --> 01:04:16,311
Eclipse! Eclipse!

1028
01:04:16,391 --> 01:04:18,535
It's eating the moon!

1029
01:04:22,951 --> 01:04:24,487
Look.

1030
01:04:31,015 --> 01:04:33,319
It's too late.

1031
01:04:37,351 --> 01:04:38,423
Tim.

1032
01:04:38,503 --> 01:04:41,111
Hey. Don't worry, big guy.

1033
01:04:41,191 --> 01:04:43,223
I'm sure the kid's OK.

1034
01:04:43,303 --> 01:04:46,007
Hey! Look over there.

1035
01:04:46,087 --> 01:04:47,655
There's another survivor!

1036
01:05:01,383 --> 01:05:03,415
It's eating everything.

1037
01:05:03,495 --> 01:05:06,135
All the stars, the luminouses...

1038
01:05:06,215 --> 01:05:07,831
and now the moon!

1039
01:05:07,911 --> 01:05:09,399
Every bit of light.

1040
01:05:09,479 --> 01:05:11,543
You're the last star...

1041
01:05:11,623 --> 01:05:13,447
and if you go...

1042
01:05:14,375 --> 01:05:16,503
Do you think I brought the shadow here?

1043
01:05:16,583 --> 01:05:17,943
I believe you, Tim.

1044
01:05:18,023 --> 01:05:20,023
You wouldn't do something like that.

1045
01:05:20,103 --> 01:05:21,543
You care about us.

1046
01:05:30,855 --> 01:05:32,055
Cat shepherd!

1047
01:05:32,135 --> 01:05:33,335
It's Tim!

1048
01:05:33,415 --> 01:05:34,743
I told you!

1049
01:05:34,823 --> 01:05:36,247
I knew he'd be OK.

1050
01:05:36,327 --> 01:05:38,263
Cat shepherd! Cat shepherd!

1051
01:05:38,343 --> 01:05:40,775
This kid's a survivor like me.

1052
01:05:48,711 --> 01:05:51,127
It's going towards Tim!

1053
01:05:51,207 --> 01:05:52,247
Cat shepherd!

1054
01:05:52,327 --> 01:05:54,535
But... it's me.

1055
01:05:59,847 --> 01:06:01,847
I hope you got a plan.

1056
01:06:01,927 --> 01:06:03,559
You'll see.

1057
01:06:06,855 --> 01:06:09,815
I don't think much of your plan!

1058
01:06:09,895 --> 01:06:12,119
Nice juicy morsel of light!

1059
01:06:12,199 --> 01:06:13,863
Not much left!

1060
01:06:17,127 --> 01:06:19,575
We did it! It's forgotten about the star.

1061
01:06:19,655 --> 01:06:22,919
Maybe it's time
we started worrying about us!

1062
01:06:31,015 --> 01:06:32,391
Where did he go?

1063
01:07:15,527 --> 01:07:16,983
OK. Come on.

1064
01:07:17,063 --> 01:07:18,743
Come on. Come and try me.

1065
01:07:18,823 --> 01:07:20,407
Come after me!

1066
01:07:20,487 --> 01:07:22,567
Come on. Don't be shy.

1067
01:07:25,607 --> 01:07:28,215
What? You chicken or something?

1068
01:07:28,295 --> 01:07:30,087
Oh, no. Not now!

1069
01:07:32,135 --> 01:07:34,647
Come on. Don't let me down now.

1070
01:07:34,727 --> 01:07:36,007
Come on!

1071
01:07:37,223 --> 01:07:38,679
Hey! Scumbag!

1072
01:07:38,759 --> 01:07:40,055
Don't you leave!

1073
01:07:40,135 --> 01:07:43,303
Don't you see what a tasty morsel I am?

1074
01:07:45,831 --> 01:07:49,271
I'm sorry, big guy. I failed.

1075
01:07:49,351 --> 01:07:51,991
No time for that now.

1076
01:07:52,071 --> 01:07:54,167
Listen, we have to hide.

1077
01:07:54,247 --> 01:07:55,799
We need to find a safe place...

1078
01:07:55,879 --> 01:07:59,047
somewhere the shadow
would never think of looking.

1079
01:08:01,383 --> 01:08:03,127
There's no such place.

1080
01:08:03,207 --> 01:08:05,479
Not anymore.

1081
01:08:17,991 --> 01:08:20,087
Where do you think you're going?

1082
01:08:20,167 --> 01:08:21,575
It won't be that easy.

1083
01:08:40,743 --> 01:08:43,431
Tim, you mustn't be afraid.

1084
01:08:44,583 --> 01:08:46,551
- He needs us! - I can't.

1085
01:08:46,631 --> 01:08:47,879
Trust me.

1086
01:08:49,127 --> 01:08:52,087
You have to... face him.

1087
01:08:52,167 --> 01:08:54,119
You have to do something!

1088
01:08:57,767 --> 01:09:00,743
You have to... face him.

1089
01:09:01,703 --> 01:09:03,159
Shepherd!

1090
01:09:03,239 --> 01:09:04,279
No!

1091
01:09:04,359 --> 01:09:05,559
Here, monster!

1092
01:09:05,639 --> 01:09:08,967
Hey! Come on,
pick on someone your own size!

1093
01:09:15,847 --> 01:09:17,111
Cat shepherd...

1094
01:09:17,191 --> 01:09:18,903
you're gonna be all right!

1095
01:09:18,983 --> 01:09:20,663
I know you are!

1096
01:09:20,743 --> 01:09:21,879
I'm sorry.

1097
01:09:21,959 --> 01:09:24,407
I did nothing to help you.

1098
01:09:24,487 --> 01:09:26,391
You can still do it.

1099
01:09:26,471 --> 01:09:29,079
You're the one who must save Nocturna.

1100
01:09:29,159 --> 01:09:30,199
What?

1101
01:09:30,279 --> 01:09:31,415
Look at me.

1102
01:09:31,495 --> 01:09:33,335
I can't do it on my own.

1103
01:09:33,415 --> 01:09:35,191
I'm afraid.

1104
01:09:35,271 --> 01:09:37,783
What is there to be afraid of?

1105
01:09:37,863 --> 01:09:39,960
You've discovered Nocturna.

1106
01:09:40,040 --> 01:09:43,447
You'd never seen us,
but we were always there.

1107
01:09:43,527 --> 01:09:45,591
You've nothing to fear.

1108
01:09:45,671 --> 01:09:48,151
Those who love you never leave you.

1109
01:09:48,231 --> 01:09:50,183
You always carry them with you...

1110
01:09:52,263 --> 01:09:53,735
even when they're not there.

1111
01:09:58,215 --> 01:09:59,591
No!

1112
01:10:00,935 --> 01:10:03,063
Don't leave me!

1113
01:10:03,143 --> 01:10:04,695
Cat shepherd.

1114
01:10:04,775 --> 01:10:06,967
Cat shepherd!

1115
01:10:07,047 --> 01:10:09,255
Cat shepherd...

1116
01:10:26,087 --> 01:10:28,135
We have to get out of here!

1117
01:10:33,095 --> 01:10:34,903
What are you doing? Run!

1118
01:10:34,983 --> 01:10:36,839
There's nowhere to run.

1119
01:10:38,407 --> 01:10:40,231
Is this what you want?

1120
01:10:42,951 --> 01:10:46,759
If I'm not afraid, he doesn't exist!

1121
01:10:57,255 --> 01:10:58,951
North Star?

1122
01:11:00,039 --> 01:11:02,407
I sure hope this works.

1123
01:11:08,360 --> 01:11:10,103
Are you OK?

1124
01:11:10,183 --> 01:11:11,767
I'm...

1125
01:11:11,847 --> 01:11:13,111
I'm shining!

1126
01:11:13,191 --> 01:11:15,367
And beautiful!

1127
01:11:42,823 --> 01:11:44,727
Tim, are you OK?

1128
01:11:44,807 --> 01:11:46,167
Yes.

1129
01:11:46,247 --> 01:11:47,671
He's gone.

1130
01:11:47,751 --> 01:11:49,991
But he'll always be with me.

1131
01:11:51,655 --> 01:11:54,039
That was some trip.

1132
01:11:54,119 --> 01:11:55,495
Tobermory!

1133
01:11:57,223 --> 01:12:00,055
Thanks for helping me, my friends.

1134
01:12:00,135 --> 01:12:02,167
Look at the sky!

1135
01:12:02,247 --> 01:12:04,327
We made it!

1136
01:12:09,831 --> 01:12:11,991
Back to work, boys.

1137
01:12:12,071 --> 01:12:13,255
OK!

1138
01:12:44,839 --> 01:12:47,959
What sort of a night have you had, champ?

1139
01:12:48,039 --> 01:12:49,143
Pretty hectic.

1140
01:12:49,223 --> 01:12:51,511
That shadow, he kept us busy,

1141
01:12:51,591 --> 01:12:52,823
but in the end...

1142
01:12:52,903 --> 01:12:54,711
Yeah, yeah. Good old Murray.

1143
01:12:54,791 --> 01:12:57,607
You're a real mean guy, right?

1144
01:13:05,639 --> 01:13:08,280
Now everything is back where it should be.

1145
01:13:08,360 --> 01:13:10,583
Almost. You belong up there.

1146
01:13:10,663 --> 01:13:14,775
Thanks for saving me,
for saving all of us.

1147
01:13:14,855 --> 01:13:16,759
It was great being with you.

1148
01:13:16,839 --> 01:13:18,071
Say hello to Adhara.

1149
01:13:18,151 --> 01:13:21,143
Thank her for being
there night after night.

1150
01:13:21,223 --> 01:13:22,391
Good-bye!

1151
01:13:22,471 --> 01:13:24,839
I'll be keeping an eye on you.

1152
01:13:37,895 --> 01:13:39,479
I know, I know.

1153
01:13:39,559 --> 01:13:40,775
It's time for bed.

1154
01:13:45,703 --> 01:13:47,575
You've been a perfect guardian.

1155
01:13:47,655 --> 01:13:48,727
I'm sure the shepherd

1156
01:13:48,807 --> 01:13:50,311
would be very proud of you.

1157
01:14:13,640 --> 01:14:16,279
I'd just like to say thanks to all of you.

1158
01:14:16,359 --> 01:14:18,615
It's been a long night's work...

1159
01:14:18,695 --> 01:14:21,959
and we could use a good day's rest.

1160
01:14:28,583 --> 01:14:29,591
Me, me!

1161
01:14:29,671 --> 01:14:31,575
Pass it to me! No, no, come on!

1162
01:14:31,655 --> 01:14:34,647
Shoot it, shoot it!

1163
01:14:34,727 --> 01:14:36,247
It's not fair!

1164
01:14:36,327 --> 01:14:38,791
Pass it, pass it!

